window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>Fate makes no exceptions<b>.</b><br> <br> When stepping into a town full of werewolves like me for the first time in my life, I expected to be welcomed—or at least tolerated.<br> <br> Instead, I got hit in the face with a door.<br> <br> And then, found my dad's face on a dartboard in their diner.<br> <br> The people there need my help, but I can't help them unless I tell them who I am. And telling them who I am just might get me killed.<br> <br> The one connection I find comes in the form of a gorgeous, inked-up chemist who's the only person in town that doesn't hate me. He could be exactly what I need in more ways that one—and I'm pretty sure he's my fated mate.<br> <br> Every day I'm there seems to increase my odds of dying as the townies try to force me out, but I refuse to back down.<br> <br> I'll save them, even if they kill me for doing it.</p> <p>This new-adult paranormal romance is recommended for ages 17 and up due to language and sexual content. It contains the complete Moon of the Monsters trilogy, including <i>Where the</i> <i>Werewolves Run, Where the Lycans Howl,</i> and <i>Where the Monsters Change.</i></p>"; 
